  "notes": [
    "fresh = first valuation at a spot never evaluated before on this solved basis; hot = repeated valuation at a visited spot (for the Mathieu basis this hits a per-(mu, nu) memo of the special-function values; Bessel and Fourier have no such memo).",
    "greeks = price, delta1, delta2, theta, gamma1, gamma2, gamma12. Deltas and theta are analytic; gammas central-difference the analytic gradient with a log-price step of 1e-4, which evaluates the gradient at four further spots.",
    "greeks_full adds vega1, vega2 and rho by central differences over six re-solved markets (vol bump 0.01, rate bump 1e-4).",
    "batch = vectorised valuation over the interior points of a 50 x 50 grid, through the basis's design matrix; checked against the scalar path at five points.",
    "fdm = one monolithic Crank-Nicolson solve, 4 Rannacher steps, Shortley-Weller boundary, N = 320, 500 time steps."
  ],
